 1. Why we cannot automate CAPTCHA using selenium?

CAPTCHA (Completely Automated Public Turing test to tell Computers and Humans Apart) is designed to prevent automated scripts, including Selenium, from accessing a website. 
CAPTCHA uses advanced algorithms to generate distorted images or audio that are difficult for machines to decipher, but easy for humans to recognize. 
Selenium can't automate CAPTCHA because it's meant to distinguish humans from bots.

2. Write a program to open Opera browser

package seleniumpractice;
import org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver;
import org.openqa.selenium.opera.OperaDriver;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.setProperty("webdriver.opera.driver", "/path/to/operadriver");
        WebDriver driver = new OperaDriver();
        driver.get("https://www.google.com");
    }
}



3. What is the difference between driver.quit() and driver.close()

driver.close() : Closes the current browser window.
driver.quit() : Closes all browser windows and terminates the WebDriver session.



4.Explain about WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver(). Why we assign the Object of chrome driver to webdriver reference?

WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver(); is an example of polymorphism in Java.  
ChromeDriver is a concrete implementation of the WebDriver  interface. 
